  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID-Wildlife Security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to strengthen the enforcement of forestry and wildlife laws by exposing serious offences in the forestry sector; prosecuting illegal forestry exploiters and wildlife traffickers; and increasing national capacity to apply forestry and wildlife laws in Gabon. The project will: Identify the main operators in illegal forestry and establish clear evidence against them; Facilitate the arrests of these suspects; Follow-up their cases until prosecution and beyond so that court rulings are executed; Draw the attention of the public and, in particular, people in forestry to the new status quo of effective enforcement of forestry law; and Organize trainings for specific personnel of the Ministry of Water as well as for Customs, Justice and Forces of Law and Order regarding forestry legislation and penal procedures.</narrative>
  </description>
